Make the cap continuous at the kept print. Use the engine's own Poncelet law, which has kr = K.PONCELET_K x rho, not bare rho. Use the blow's own momentum formula (leg plus extra stamp mass), not m·v alone. In MOVES.stomp.blow replace the cap line with:

const T = footPulse(o.body), q = qultFor(o.surface, o.body.footB), kr = K.PONCELET_K * (o.surface.rho || 2000), pc = r.printCap || 0;
const vP = pc > 0 ? Math.sqrt(q / kr * Math.expm1(2 * kr * o.body.footArea * pc / o.body.legEff)) : 0;
const Jp = momentumOf(vP, o.body.legEff) + Math.max(0, stampMass(o.body) - o.body.legEff) * Math.min(vP, stampSpeed(o.body));
const cap = Math.max(q * o.body.footArea * T, Jp);

Verified on a patched copy (fpatch.js / fpatch2.js):
- The stomp is monotonic on all nine surfaces.
- Sand holds 6,395 kg·m/s (12.2 mm/s at 5 m) from the print up to 10^10 kg, and plasterOver at 1.5 m stays true.
- Clay (print 0) is unchanged at the static cap.
- The powers-off path is untouched.

Add a powers-on check to test/powers.js that the stomp's ppv at 5 m never falls as effort rises, on sand, gravel, soft clay and concrete.

Cap only where real ground gives, and keep the cap continuous at the threshold. At landRatioReal = 1 the landing speed is v1 = sqrt(2 d landBear / m), and the ground demonstrably bears the feet's blow 2 legEff v1. In MOVES.jump.shake:

const v1 = r.landBear != null ? Math.sqrt(2 * o.body.strokes.leg * r.landBear / o.m) : 0;
const cap = (J, T, J1) => (o.unbreakable && r.landBear != null && r.landRatioReal > 1 ? Math.min(J, Math.max(r.landBear * T, J1 || 0)) : J);

The feet's entry becomes cap(2 * o.body.legEff * L.v, footPulse(o.body), 2 * o.body.legEff * v1). The body pulse keeps cap(momentumOf(L.v, o.m), L.t), which is already continuous.

Verified on a patched copy (fpatch.js patched): on all nine surfaces the borne landing equals the uncapped value and the landing shaking is monotonic. Extend the powers.js jump check to sand and soft clay.

Use a module-level flag set only while the real-ground bay draws. Next to 'let duoMode = false;' add: let duoRealDraw = false;

In renderInto:
if (duoEff && duoEff.real) { state.unbreakable = false; duoRealDraw = ub; }
try { parts = ... } finally { state.unbreakable = ub; duoRealDraw = false; }

In collideCharge:
const r = P.collide(cA, cB, { source: state.colSrc, gb, bounce: state.colBounce === 'bounce', toGround: duoRealDraw }), out = [];

Also drop '(Unbreakable footing)' from the math line's 'Ground shaking (Unbreakable footing)' when duoRealDraw is set.

